Root cause:
The bug was caused by the failure to clear all skb (socket buffer) extensions during the scrubbing process and when freeing or reusing skb in the NAPI (New API) context. Specifically, the existing code only cleared the secpath extension, leaving other extensions like the tc (traffic control) extension intact. This could lead to inconsistencies and potential security issues, as stale or incorrect extension data could be retained in the skb. The patch introduces a new helper function to ensure that all extensions are properly cleared, addressing this oversight.
